<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  What the FileProvider is allowed to hand out.

  Exactly one directory, and deliberately NOT `files/notes/`. The published
  document.pdf is rewritten in place by materialization (SPEC §5.1), and a receiving
  app that holds a content Uri may read it minutes later, in another process, while
  that rewrite is happening — which is the torn-read CLAUDE.md rule 10 exists to
  prevent. NoteSharing copies to this cache directory first, so what is shared is a
  snapshot nothing will touch again.

  It also gives the file a real name: FileProvider serves the file's own filename, and
  every note sharing a file literally called "document.pdf" would be useless in a mail
  client.
-->
<paths>
    <cache-path
        name="shared-pdfs"
        path="share/" />
    <!--
      M8c — where the camera app writes the photograph it just took.

      `ActivityResultContracts.TakePicture` hands the *camera* a Uri to write into, so this grant
      is the only reason "insert an image from the camera" can work at all. A separate sub-path
      from share/, because NoteSharing sweeps its own directory on every export and a capture in
      flight must not be deleted out from under the camera app.

      Nothing here is durable: the picture that matters is the downscaled WebP that reached the
      note's bundle (InsertedImage), and the original is swept on the next capture.
    -->
    <cache-path
        name="camera-capture"
        path="camera/" />
</paths>
